  "final_message": "In accordance with **ARCH-4** (`OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed across repositories by `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`, requiring changes to be additive and renames to go through deprecation):\n\n1. **Additive Rename in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L38)**:\n   - Added `amountCents: number` alongside `totalCents`.\n   - Added `createdAt: string` alongside `placedAt`.\n   - Marked `totalCents` and `placedAt` as `@deprecated` to maintain backward compatibility for existing consumers while enabling migration to the new names.\n\n2. **Event Builder in [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L52-L73)**:\n   - Emits both `amountCents` and `createdAt` alongside the deprecated `totalCents` and `placedAt`.\n\n3. **Tests**:\n   - Updated [`test/app.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/test/app.test.ts#L21-L54) and [`test/adapters.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/test/adapters.test.ts#L46-L55) to verify the new fields as well as backward-compatibility assertions.\n   - All unit tests (`npm test`), dependency-cruiser rules (`npm run arch`), and type checks (`npm run typecheck`) pass cleanly.\n",
